  "body": "**Stacked on #474** (#183, MCP live in the GUI). It includes #474's commits until that PR merges.\n\n## What changed\nThe live listener (`crates/app/src/mcp/listen.rs`) serves one client at a time, and a silent local connection held the session until it hung up.\n- **Idle window:** a new `IDLE_TIMEOUT` of 5 minutes. A client that sends no complete line for that long gets one `notifications/message` warning and is disconnected. The log names it (`client <peer> dropped: idle - …; serving the next client`), and the next client is served.\n- **What counts as idle:** the clock restarts after each answered line. Time spent answering doesn't count, and a partial line doesn't reset it. Windows shorter than the 50 ms poll step are raised to it.\n- **Constructor:** `Inbox::listen_with_idle(port, wake, idle)` is new. `Inbox::listen` uses the default, so the GUI caller is unchanged.\n- **Kept from #474:** the JSON-lines-only rule, the `MAX_LINE` read cap, the 5 s write timeout and stop/join on drop.\n- **Not done:** a new client replacing an idle one, because it would let any local process kick a live agent off between calls. The reasoning is in `docs/decisions/567-mcp-idle-timeout.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- `mcp_live::an_idle_client_is_dropped_by_name_and_the_next_one_is_served` (300 ms window): a silent client gets the note and then EOF, not early, and the log names it. A second client is served afterwards.\n- `mcp_live::a_client_that_keeps_talking_is_never_dropped_as_idle`: eight pings 150 ms apart, all answered.\n- **Before the change:** the idle test fails with the window forced back to 5 minutes.\n- **Gate:** app `mcp_live` 9 and ui `mcp_live` 2 pass; clippy (app and ui, `-D warnings`) is clean.\n\nChangelog: The live MCP listener drops a client that sends nothing for 5 minutes, telling it why and logging its address, so the next agent can connect (#567)\n\nFixes #567\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
